# netsurf: Vita clipping on the CPU, clock control, run-4 autotest (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# Hardware run 3 (doc 10): 12-69 ms of GPU per frame, growing with the draw.
# vita2d clips with the stencil, and every vita2d_set_clip_rectangle() --
# vita2d_enable_clipping() calls it too -- rewrites it: a full 960x544 fill
# plus the clip rect. The plotter called both per core clip (30-160 a frame).
# - plot.c: clipping moves to the CPU. Axis-aligned fills are intersected
#   with the clip exactly, primitives wholly outside are skipped, wholly
#   inside need nothing, and only a primitive crossing the clip edge uses the
#   stencil, rewritten only when the clip changed. The old behaviour stays
#   selectable (VITA_CLIP_STENCIL) for measuring. Per-frame counters.
# - diag.c: logs ARM/bus/GPU/crossbar clocks at boot; vita_diag_set_clocks().
# - main.c: the browsing profile is CPU clipping + GPU 222 MHz; the autotest
#   runs 4 passes (A boot clocks + stencil clip, B GPU 222 + stencil,
#   C boot clocks + CPU clip, D ARM 444/bus 222/GPU 222 + CPU clip), each
#   page timed over 5 frames, with per-pass summaries in log.txt.
# - Makefile: -DVITA_HOST_SIM for the simulator build (snapshot hook, so the
#   simulator can compare the clip modes pixel for pixel).
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 4.

